<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · infrastructure</p><h1 class="enc-title">Emperor Ferdinand Northern Railway</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1837</span> · Also known as Kaiser Ferdinands-Nordbahn</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Emperor Ferdinand Northern Railway was the first steam railway in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austrian-empire">Austrian Empire</a>, financed by Salomon Rothschild and opened in 1837 between Floridsdorf and Deutsch-Wagram near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a>. It reached <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brno">Brünn</a> in 1839 and was extended to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coal">coal</a> fields of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moravia">Moravia</a> and Silesia and to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galicia">Galicia</a>, becoming one of the most profitable railways of the monarchy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/emperor-ferdinand-northern-railway.jpg" alt="Emperor Ferdinand Northern Railway" width="320" height="184" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gaj777 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dworzec_G%C5%82%C3%B3wny_-_detal_fasady.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
